.vercel
# `.claude/` holds team tooling (settings, hooks, agent definitions, output
# styles) tracked by default; only the paths below are local-agent state.
.codex/skills
.github/skills
.claude/worktrees
.claude/skills
.claude/settings.local.json
# Driver runtime artifacts: chosen ports + the Chromium profile it drives with.
.agents/skills/*/.state.json
.agents/skills/*/.state.json.tmp
.agents/skills/*/.chrome-profile/
# The repros and the screenshots the drive-* skills tell a session to write
# into the checkout root, whatever they are named, so `git add -A` cannot
# sweep them into a commit. Nothing tracked lives at the root under either
# extension.
/*.sd
/*.png
.spark
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/out/

# npm workspaces: only the root lockfile is authoritative. Ignore stray
# per-package lockfiles created by running `npm install` inside a workspace.
**/package-lock.json
!/package-lock.json

# Vite writes a transient timestamped copy of a config next to it whenever the
# config is a TS module; these accumulate and are never source.
**/*.timestamp-*.mjs
